  "description": "A study in Nature, led by Boston Children's Hospital and Harvard, sequenced single neurons from donated human brains. The authors report that about 26% of prenatal cortical neurons carried large chromosome changes, falling to about 6% after birth, and suggest those neurons are selectively removed. The work was done on postmortem brains of people without a neurological diagnosis.\n\nSources: Nature paper (Shao et al., Oct 28) and Nature news; News-Medical; GEN; Neuroscience News.\n\n#science #neuroscience #brain #nature",
